        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Per <a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/mdn/discussions/857\">https://github.com/orgs/mdn/discussions/857</a>, this PR deletes the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Insecure_passwords\" rel=\"nofollow\">Insecure passwords</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Weak_Signature_Algorithm\" rel=\"nofollow\">Weak signature algorithms</a> pages, redirecting to better sources.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It seems like the \"Insecure passwords\" page used to have something about Firefox warning about insecure forms, but the page has not had anything on this at least since the GitHub migration (<a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdn/content/bf1d03163546071f07e8b33eefdbd1d4dec19940/files/en-us/web/security/insecure_passwords/index.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">here's</a> the initial commit of that page) so I just removed any links that promised this information.</p>",
