        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20392302?u=5dcac116a63e4eaf0fd7243fdf8e9139962831ae&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">…of $(\"&lt;/div&gt;\")</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Corrected HTML tag in jQuery example for clarity.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41907",
            "title": "docs(WebExtensions): fix jQuery example typo, use $(\"<div>\") instead …",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-12T01:29:12.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-12T01:27:29.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ajayojha",
                "url": "https://github.com/ajayojha"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 146 onwards has the <code class=\"notranslate\">text-decoration-inset</code> property enabled by default (see <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1993043\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1993043</a>; it was called <code class=\"notranslate\">text-decoration-trim</code>, but it got renamed). I've tested it, and it doesn't work in Chrome/Safari yet.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a reference page for the new property, and links to it from the text decoration module page.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41901",
            "title": "Add docs for the CSS text-decoration-inset property",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-13T10:05:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-11T12:41:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It’s an automation script that helps to create Firefox release notes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I created the <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41896\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41896/hovercard\">Firefox 145 release notes PR</a> using this script.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To simplify release notes workflow.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How it works, for example, with the newly released Firefox 145:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"node scripts/release-firefox.js 145\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">node scripts/release-firefox.js 145</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What it does:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Takes the newly released version as a parameter (N), and:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Removes active from N-1</li>\n<li>Updates N to Stable\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Uncomments HTML, CSS, JavaScript “no notable changes” sections</li>\n<li>Removes all other unused commented sections</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Updates N+1 to Beta</li>\n<li>Adds Nightly N+2 page</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For release dates, it uses official JSON API — <a href=\"https://whattrainisitnow.com/api/firefox/calendar/future/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://whattrainisitnow.com/api/firefox/calendar/future/</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3610323814\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41896\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41896/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41896\">#41896</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41897",
            "title": "Add Firefox release automation script",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-11T08:42:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-11T01:47:46.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pepelsbey",
                "url": "https://github.com/pepelsbey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The \"Visual Viewport API\" sidebar has been removed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3267000779\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40547\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40547/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40547\">#40547</a>. This PR removes the last remnant, which is the landing page, by subsuming its information into <code class=\"notranslate\">VisualViewport</code>. It also removes links to a nonexistent API \"Viewport API\". I'm not sure how this even got into MDN: perhaps the <code class=\"notranslate\">Viewport</code> interface was meant.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41893",
            "title": "\"Viewport API\" and \"Visual Viewport API\" are not real specs",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-10T15:12:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-10T15:09:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Syncs the <code class=\"notranslate\">SECURITY.md</code> file with the <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/blob/main/SECURITY.md\">canonical version from mdn/fred</a>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Ensures consistent security reporting procedures across all MDN repositories.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See: <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/getting-started/adding-a-security-policy-to-your-repository\">https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/getting-started/adding-a-security-policy-to-your-repository</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3607054758\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1068\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/fred/issues/1068/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1068\">mdn/fred#1068</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41892",
            "title": "docs(SECURITY): sync security policy",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-10T15:52:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-10T15:08:36.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 143 adds support for the WebGPU <a href=\"https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#dom-gpufeaturename-texture-component-swizzle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">texture-component-swizzle</code></a> feature, which, when enabled, allows usage of the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GPUTexture/createView\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">createView()</code></a> method's <a href=\"https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#dom-gputextureviewdescriptor-swizzle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">swizzle</code></a> option that allows developers to perform color swizzles.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5110223547269120\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5110223547269120</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds documentation for both the feature and the option.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41841",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document WebGPU texture view swizzle feature",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-13T07:53:06.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-07T17:40:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Use of the <code class=\"notranslate\">bgra8unorm</code> format for read-only storage textures is deprecated. The specification explicitly disallows this, as this format is intended for write-only access and is not portable. Any browser support for this combination is considered a bug.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome previously allowed this, but it is deprecated from version 140 onwards. See <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-140#deprecate_bgra8unorm_read-only_storage_texture_usage\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-140#deprecate_bgra8unorm_read-only_storage_texture_usage</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a note to make the deprecation clear. Note that I'm not intending to add a browser compat data point for this change, as:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>It is expected behavior anyway.</li>\n<li>We don't really want to encourage people to use it in browsers that wrongly allow it.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41840",
            "title": "Editorial review: Add note about bgra8unorm read-only storage textures bring deprecated",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-07T15:36:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-07T15:14:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        }
    ]
}